  "id": "operant-learning",
  "term": "operant learning",
  "definition": "Operant learning is a way behavior is shaped by its consequences, especially by patterns of reinforcement. The packet supports that when reinforcement is given only some of the time rather than every time, the behavior can become more resistant to fading when reinforcement stops.",
